<main id="main" class="wrap">
  <div class="page-head">
    <h2>Dashboard</h2>
    <p class="lede">Profile this research answers for: a U.S. citizen living in California (assumed ages 19&ndash;64), with <strong>$0 earned income</strong>, whose money comes from <strong>Kalshi trading</strong>, <strong>rental property</strong>, and <strong>savings interest</strong>. Personal facts are never assumed &mdash; see <a href="flagged-for-review.html">Flagged for Review</a>.</p>
    <p class="kbd-note">This is the expanded data dashboard (110 sourced rows, generated from <code>data/*.csv</code>). A shorter companion research brief by a parallel session is published at the <a href="../index.html">site root</a>.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="qa-grid">
    <div class="qa">
      <h3>Do I need earned income to get covered?</h3>
      <p><strong>No.</strong> Both Medi-Cal and Covered California measure your household MAGI &mdash; which already counts your rental, interest, and trading income. Neither program requires a job or wages.</p>
      <p class="more"><a href="medi-cal.html">Medi-Cal &rarr;</a> &nbsp; <a href="covered-california.html">Covered California &rarr;</a></p>
    </div>
    <div class="qa">
      <h3>Can I keep Medi-Cal in 2027 with $0 earned income?</h3>
      <p><strong>Yes.</strong> The new work rule counts hours or income &mdash; not employment &mdash; and California tests <strong>any one month</strong> per renewal period, not every month. Meet that month with <strong>$580 MAGI-based income from any source</strong> (net rent + interest + trading gains), <strong>80&nbsp;hours of structured community service</strong>, <strong>half-time school</strong>, a work program, a combination, or an exemption.</p>
      <p class="more"><a href="work-requirements.html">Work requirements &rarr;</a></p>
    </div>
    <div class="qa">
      <h3>What is the new law, and when does it take effect?</h3>
      <p>Section 71119 of the One Big Beautiful Bill Act (P.L.&nbsp;119&ndash;21, signed July 4, 2025), implemented by a CMS rule issued June 1, 2026. States must implement by <strong>January 1, 2027</strong>; California starts six-month checks March 1, 2027.</p>
      <p class="more"><a href="work-requirements.html">Full details &rarr;</a></p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section aria-labelledby="numbers-h">
    <h3 id="numbers-h">Key numbers (2026 / 2027 coverage year)</h3>
    <div class="tiles">
      <div class="tile"><div class="num">80 hrs</div><div class="lbl">monthly qualifying activity standard</div></div>
      <div class="tile"><div class="num">$580</div><div class="lbl">MAGI-based income in a qualifying month (any source)</div></div>
      <div class="tile"><div class="num">$22,025</div><div class="lbl">Medi-Cal limit, household of 1 (138% FPL, 2026)</div></div>
      <div class="tile"><div class="num">100&ndash;400%</div><div class="lbl">FPL range for federal premium tax credits</div></div>
      <div class="tile"><div class="num">$31,920</div><div class="lbl">CA state subsidy ceiling, household of 1 (200% FPL, 2027)</div></div>
      <div class="tile"><div class="num">Nov 1, 2026</div><div class="lbl">Covered California open enrollment opens</div></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="findings-h">
    <h3 id="findings-h">Key findings</h3>
    <div class="panel accent">
      <ol>
        <li><strong>$0 earned income does not block coverage.</strong> MAGI &mdash; used by both Medi-Cal and the marketplace &mdash; counts interest, capital gains, and net rental income alongside wages. <a href="income-treatment.html">Income &amp; MAGI &rarr;</a></li>
        <li><strong>Medi-Cal today:</strong> adults 19&ndash;64 with household MAGI at or below 138% FPL ($22,025/yr for one person in 2026) qualify with <strong>no asset test, no premium, and no work requirement</strong> &mdash; nothing about work changes until January 1, 2027. <a href="medi-cal.html">Medi-Cal &rarr;</a></li>
        <li><strong>The new work rule is not an earned-income test.</strong> From January 1, 2027, Medi-Cal expansion adults must show 80 hours/month of qualifying activity &mdash; or monthly income of at least $580 <em>from any source</em> (DHCS), or an exemption. Unpaid community service and half-time school count. <a href="work-requirements.html">Details &rarr;</a></li>
        <li><strong>If MAGI is 138&ndash;400% FPL:</strong> Covered California has <strong>no work requirement at all</strong> &mdash; federal premium tax credits, state subsidies (up to 200% FPL for 2027), and Silver cost-sharing reductions (up to 250% FPL). <a href="covered-california.html">Covered California &rarr;</a></li>
        <li><strong>Enhanced federal subsidies expired December 31, 2025</strong> &mdash; the 400% FPL cliff is back. A House-passed three-year extension (H.R. 1834) is stalled in the Senate as of this snapshot. <a href="covered-california.html">Status &rarr;</a></li>
        <li><strong>California's response:</strong> AB 2161 (signed September 14, 2026) requires counties to verify from data before paperwork, keep coverage alive during the 30-day response window, and check every other eligibility basis before cutting anyone. <a href="work-requirements.html">California rollout &rarr;</a></li>
        <li><strong>Transparency:</strong> {{STAT_FLAGGED}} items are flagged for review &mdash; values that could not be confirmed from an official source (left blank) plus inconsistencies found between official pages. <a href="flagged-for-review.html">Flagged for Review &rarr;</a></li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="timeline-h">
    <h3 id="timeline-h">Timeline</h3>
    <ul class="timeline">
      <li><span class="when">July 4, 2025</span> One Big Beautiful Bill Act (P.L. 119-21) signed; section 71119 creates Medicaid work &amp; community engagement requirements; section 71107 creates six-month renewals.</li>
      <li><span class="when">December 8, 2025</span> CMS issues initial implementation guidance to states.</li>
      <li><span class="when">December 31, 2025</span> Enhanced ACA premium tax credits expire; the 400% FPL subsidy cliff returns for 2026 coverage.</li>
      <li><span class="when">January 8, 2026</span> House passes H.R. 1834 (three-year enhanced-credit extension), 230&ndash;196; Senate action still pending as of this snapshot.</li>
      <li><span class="when">June 1, 2026</span> CMS issues interim final rule CMS-2454-IFC (published June 3; effective July 31, 2026).</li>
      <li><span class="when">Aug&ndash;Dec 2026</span> DHCS mails Medi-Cal member outreach letters (from late August); counties include them with applications October 1 &ndash; December 31, 2026.</li>
      <li><span class="when">November 1, 2026</span> Covered California open enrollment for 2027 coverage begins (through January 31, 2027).</li>
      <li><span class="when">January 1, 2027</span> Work &amp; community engagement rules take effect for Medi-Cal expansion adults; retroactive coverage shortens to one month for childless adults.</li>
      <li><span class="when">March 1, 2027</span> Six-month eligibility checks begin in California; existing members are assessed at renewal.</li>
      <li><span class="when">October 1, 2028</span> New Medi-Cal copayments for some adults (capped at 5% of household income) begin.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

